* aif120_lock_contract_regression.dts
* AIF-120 (application-ui-dsl) -- the lane's lock contract, expressed in the house's
* own script language instead of a bespoke harness.
*
* Why this file exists: rulings R47 through R63 proved the lock contract with C++
* probes, Python harnesses and WSL shell scripts. DotTalk++ already ships a script
* language, a regression launcher and a self-asserting proof form. This is the same
* contract restated where the house keeps its proofs. See AIF120_DOTSCRIPT_V1.md.
*
* Form: transcript canary (the comment_handling_regression.dts form), not the
* "<TAG>:.T." form -- lock state is not reachable from the expression path, so the
* proof is the documented expected output below, read against the run.
*
* Fixture: STUDENTS and ENROLL from the shipped x64 school tables. Read-only:
* nothing is appended, replaced, deleted or packed. Every lock taken is released.
*
* Regression doctrine: every test sets its own environment.
*
* Run:  DOTSCRIPT aif120\aif120_lock_contract_regression.dts
*
* EXPECTED OUTPUT (the assertion; * marks the line that carries a claim):
*   A3 -- Table: LOCKED  AND  Record 5: unlocked        (R54: independent by design)
*   A4 -- UNLOCK prints a RECORD message and the table stays LOCKED  (correction 34)
*   B1 -- owner token is host:pid:ms, with no user and no session   (R54 open item)
*   C1 -- UNLOCK reports "unlocked" for a record that was never locked
*   C2 -- ...while LOCK WHO on the same record says "no lock recorded"
*   D1 -- LOCK twice on one record reports success twice, no depth count  (R51)
*   D2 -- ...and ONE UNLOCK releases it
*   E1 -- LOCK STATUS reports the CURRENT record, not the record that is locked
*   F1 -- two work areas hold two table locks at once  (R26 lock domain)

SET ECHO OFF
STOP_ON_ERROR OFF
SET PATH DBF dbf/x64

FORMULA "AIF120-LOCK-CONTRACT-BEGIN"

ECHO
ECHO --- A. the record verb and the table verb are not symmetric ---
SELECT 1
USE STUDENTS
GOTO 5
ECHO A1 LOCK
LOCK
LOCK STATUS
ECHO A2 UNLOCK
UNLOCK
LOCK STATUS
ECHO A3 LOCK TABLE
LOCK TABLE
LOCK STATUS
ECHO A4 UNLOCK -- claims the record, leaves the table
UNLOCK
LOCK STATUS
ECHO A5 UNLOCK TABLE
UNLOCK TABLE
LOCK STATUS

ECHO
ECHO --- B. the owner token ---
LOCK
ECHO B1 LOCK WHO 5
LOCK WHO 5
UNLOCK

ECHO
ECHO --- C. an unlock that measures nothing ---
ECHO C1 UNLOCK 77 with no lock held
UNLOCK 77
ECHO C2 LOCK WHO 77
LOCK WHO 77

ECHO
ECHO --- D. re-entrancy carries no depth ---
ECHO D1 LOCK 9 twice
LOCK 9
LOCK 9
ECHO D2 UNLOCK 9 once
UNLOCK 9
LOCK WHO 9

ECHO
ECHO --- E. LOCK STATUS follows the cursor, not the lock ---
GOTO 7
LOCK 9
ECHO E1 LOCK STATUS at record 7 while record 9 is locked
LOCK STATUS
LOCK WHO 9
UNLOCK 9

ECHO
ECHO --- F. two areas, two table locks (R26 lock domain) ---
SELECT 2
USE ENROLL
LOCK TABLE
LOCK STATUS
SELECT 1
LOCK TABLE
LOCK STATUS
ECHO F1 both areas report a table lock above
UNLOCK TABLE
SELECT 2
UNLOCK TABLE
LOCK STATUS

WORKSPACE CLOSE

FORMULA "AIF120-LOCK-CONTRACT-END"
